{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\23201\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -NoProfile -Command \"Get-ChildItem -Force -Name\nGet-Content -LiteralPath '.agents\\\\skills\\\\matlab-runner\\\\references\\\\mcp-readiness-ladder.md','.agents\\\\skills\\\\matlab-runner\\\\references\\\\acceptance-levels.md' -Raw\nrg --files --hidden -g '\"'!'\"\\\\.git/**' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'AGENT.md' -g 'CLAUDE.md' -g '*Test-MatlabMcpExistingSession*' -g '*mas_route*' -g '*acceptance-report.schema.json' -g '*routing.json'\"","aggregated_output":".agents\r\n# MCP readiness ladder\n\nLoaded on demand by `matlab-runner`. The Agent does not need this table unless it is\nabout to claim MCP is ready �� which is exactly the claim that must not be made from\na config file.\n\n## A config check is not a readiness check\n\nA `sessionDetails.json` on disk, a listening PID, or a client entry in `.mcp.json`\nall look identical to a file-existence test and all prove nothing about whether a\ntool call will work. There are at least five distinct states, and only the fourth\nmeans \"usable\":\n\n| # | State | Looks fine? | Actually means |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | server process not running | yes | nothing is listening |\n| 2 | process running, wrong port | yes | the client will connect to the wrong thing |\n| 3 | handshake rejected | yes | auth or protocol mismatch |\n| 4 | handshake OK, `tools/call` fails | **yes** | the only state a config check cannot detect |\n\n## The ladder\n\nRun the staged probe and read its verdict, never a file listing:\n\n```powershell\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\scripts\\Test-MatlabMcpExistingSession.ps1 -Json\n```\n\n| Stage | Check id | Level | Proves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `mcp.matlab-install` | L1 | MATLAB executable resolved, `VersionInfo.xml` readable |\n| 2 | `mcp.matlab-license` | L1 | license usable (SKIP by default, `-VerifyLicense` to force) |\n| 2 | `mcp.session-config` | L1 | session JSON parses, certificate exists, port valid |\n| 2 | `mcp.client-registration` | L2 | client args have no `display-mode`, `command` really exists |\n| 3 | `mcp.protocol-handshake` | L2 | TCP reachable and `initialize` returns a valid `result` |\n| 4 | `mcp.readonly-exec` | L3 | a read-only command really executed through `tools/call` |\n| 5 | `mcp.file-io` | L4 | token written to an isolated dir and read back identical |\n\n## Rules that must not be relaxed\n\n- **Only stage 4 passing upgrades `mcp.matlab-license` from SKIP to PASS**, and the\n  evidence (`provenBy = mcp.readonly-exec`) is recorded in `metrics`. A licence that\n  has merely not been tested is SKIP, never PASS.\n- **A failed stage makes every later stage SKIP** with reason \"upstream not passed\".\n  Never continue as if the earlier stage had succeeded �� this is how a broken\n  session produces a report full of unexplained later failures.\n- **An HTTP error must keep both the status code and the JSON-RPC error** in\n  `reason`. A bare `unauthorized` string hides the difference between \"the server\n  is down\" and \"the key is wrong\", which have opposite fixes.\n\n## Decision rule for this machine\n\n1. Prefer official MATLAB MCP auto mode, so the server reuses an existing shared\n   session or starts MATLAB automatically.\n2. Stay on MCP when the task needs repeated model edits, parameter sweeps with live\n   inspection, or anything user-visible on the desktop.\n3. Reserve `matlab -batch` for explicit requests: CI, headless smoke tests,\n   reproducible one-shot runs.\n4. If MCP is unavailable, **report the blocker**. Do not silently change execution\n   mode �� a batch rerun that succeeds hides the problem the user needs to see.\n\n## Setup\n\n```powershell\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\scripts\\Setup-MatlabMcpExistingSession.ps1\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\scripts\\Test-MatlabMcpExistingSession.ps1\n```\n\n## �Զ��򿪿ɼ� MATLAB ����\n\n�����вֿ�� `scripts/Start-MatlabDesktop.ps1`�����ȸ���ƥ������й�������ʱ��\n���洰�ڣ�û�� MATLAB ʱ�Զ��� Windows Shell �򿪿ɼ����棬�ȴ�����Ψһ\nreceipt�����ؽ��ٷ� stdio `auto` ���Ӳ�����ʵ����ִ����֤��\n�����δ����ʵ�����ȶ���������Ƿ��� `-NewSession` ���������ر��û�ԭ�Ự��\n`REUSED_EXISTING` ���������������� `newSessionVerified=true` ������ǰû��\nMATLAB ����ʱ�ſɼ�¼ `coldStartVerified=true`���˿ڡ�PID �� receipt ��������\n��������� MCP ִ����֤����� `docs/MATLAB_DESKTOP_STARTUP_ZH.md`��\n��Ҫ��ȷ�����ֶ����ʱ���� `-LaunchMode Shortcut`����ѡ���غ��ùٷ� MCP ִ��\n����ָ���� `mcpCodeFile`������ `-ConfirmReport` �˶Ի�ִ����ѡ�������������ɹ���\n����ʽ�� `-LaunchMode ComDesktop` �ɶ��� STA holder ������ע��Ŀɼ����沢���� COM ���ã�\n���� COM ���ؾ� PID ʱΪ `NOT_NEW`��������д���û��Ự��������������\nholder �����������ؽ��ٷ� stdio `auto` ����֤ʵ��ִ�У����������������˳��󸴺˳�����\n\r\n# Acceptance levels L1�CL5, and how they get upgraded\n\nLoaded on demand by `matlab-runner`. Read this before writing \"it works\".\n\n## The levels are cumulative and never automatic\n\n| Level | Meaning | Example evidence | What it does NOT prove |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 | artifact produced | `.slx` created and non-empty; `.c`/`.h` generated | that anything was compiled |\n| L2 | build/compile succeeded | MEX built; `slbuild` produced a library; model `update` passed | that the numbers are right |\n| L3 | numeric result matches | `rmse` / `maxAbsDiff` within tolerance against a golden value | that other scenarios work |\n| L4 | multi-scenario and failure modes | parameter sweep, NaN/Inf propagation, illegal size rejected | that it runs on hardware |\n| L5 | real hardware run | board download plus read-back | �� |\n\nA run that produced a file has an **L1** claim. Calling that \"deployed\" is the single\nmost common overstatement in this repository, and it is wrong in a way that survives\nreview because the file really is there.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- **File existence is an L1 claim only.** It never substitutes for L2 compile success.\n- **Generic C codegen is not STM32 deployment.** STM32 additionally needs CubeMX\n  registration, visible target hardware, a bound `.ioc`, and a matching Cube firmware\n  package. Verify each separately �� see `references/stm32-deployment-chain.md` in\n  `matlab-codegen-deploy` for the full list.\n- **Every run must edit the acceptance report** (`artifacts/validation/acceptance_report.json`),\n  which carries `status`, `command`, `exitCode`, `metrics`, `reason`, `errorClass`\n  per check.\n- **`SKIP` means \"not executed\", and it is not a pass.** A report containing any SKIP\n  has `overallStatus = SKIP` and exit code `3`.\n- **`FAIL` or `SKIP` without a `reason` is rejected by the validator at construction\n  time.** A missing reason is not a formatting nit: it is the difference between a\n  report that can be acted on and one that cannot.\n\n## Useful single checks\n\n- Unit test passes with `runtests` and `assertSuccess`.\n- Numerical tolerance check passes with **both** absolute and relative tolerance\n  recorded. One of them alone is not reproducible across scales.\n- Simulink model loads, updates, simulates to stop time, and logged signals are\n  nonempty.\n- Figure, data file, report, or generated code exists and has nonzero size (L1 only).\n- Static checks such as `checkcode` return no critical issues for touched files.\n\n## Which single checks are worth running\n\nNot all of the above are relevant to every task. The cheap ones that catch the most:\n\n| Situation | Minimum that means anything |\n|---|---|\n| pure MATLAB code | `runtests` + a numeric tolerance check with both bounds recorded |\n| Simulink model | load, `update`, simulate, and assert the logged signal is nonempty |\n| code generation | L2 build **and** L3 numeric comparison �� L2 alone says only that it compiled |\n| hardware | L5, read back from the board; a host-side loopback is L3 at best |\r\n.agents\\skills\\matlab-orchestrator\\assets\\routing.json\n.agents\\skills\\matlab-orchestrator\\scripts\\mas_route.m\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
